jorge estrada wrote:

> I found that wasting time in mine town getting all the gold was
> an accident waiting to happen with only one or two pets. 

Yes. Yes it is. I suspect that my own handling of
the racket is a bit different than what others are doing.
Here's some rules I go by:

1) When in doubt, abort. Run away, run away!
2) If you can pay the priest even once, you don't need
    to even -look- in the shops. Once is cool.
3) After paying the priest, it's time to go. Keep the
    kid gloves on as best you can until you make it to
    Dlvl 1. Now you can relax a little.
4) It's okay to abandon your pet in Minetown, if you
    need to. Turns spent there are the most dangerous
    of the dive; your primary goal at this point is to
    run the hell away.

Given special circumstances, such as a ring of invisibility
or controlled teleportitis, I'm a little more flexible
about shopping. Generally speaking though, in my mind
a perfectly executed racket involves making a slow, patient
crawl to Minetown straight through to the temple, anteing
up, then making a mad break and scrambling for the main
dungeon at almost any cost.

As usual, Your Milage May Vary.

